# Chesster1981 fork — default remote / branch

## Default (always)

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Remote | **`origin`** → `https://github.com/Chesster1981/BetterDesk.git` |
| Working branch | **`dev`** (operator’s fork) |
| Push / PR target | **Chesster1981/BetterDesk** only |

1. Before commit/push/PR: confirm `git remote -v` shows **Chesster1981**, and `git branch --show-current` is **`dev`** (or a feature branch off that fork’s `dev`).
2. **Never** open PRs, merges, or push attempts against **UNITRONIX/BetterDesk** unless Ole **explicitly** asks in that session.
3. **Never** create “upstream” PRs to UNITRONIX as a side effect of a fix (e.g. Cliprdr). Improve **Chesster1981/BetterDesk** only; close mistaken UNITRONIX PRs with a short note when asked.
4. Do **not** treat UNITRONIX issues/PRs as merge targets for this workspace — Ole closes/ignores those himself unless he orders otherwise.
5. Day-to-day commits land on **`origin/dev`** (Chesster1981). Feature branches, if used, push to Chesster1981 and stay off UNITRONIX.

## Panel Updates (Settings → Updates)

`web-nodejs/services/updateService.js` reads:

| Env | Default | Fork value |
|-----|---------|------------|
| `UPDATE_GITHUB_OWNER` | `UNITRONIX` | **`Chesster1981`** |
| `UPDATE_GITHUB_REPO` | `BetterDesk` | `BetterDesk` |
| `UPDATE_GITHUB_BRANCH` | `main` (Stable) | **`dev`** for Development channel |

Settings → Updates only switches **channel** (branch: `main` ↔ `dev`) via `setUpdateChannel` / `UPDATE_GITHUB_BRANCH`. **Owner is not in the UI** — set `UPDATE_GITHUB_OWNER=Chesster1981` in the console `.env` (and restart the console service) so Updates pull fork commits. Leaving the default `UNITRONIX` explains why Chesster-only fixes “did nothing” on Apply.

- **Do not** invent or blindly overwrite production `.env` secrets — only append/change when Ole asks (`envMerge` / `upsertEnvKey` patterns).

## Release exception (UNITRONIX)

When Ole **explicitly** asks for an upstream / production release to UNITRONIX, follow [`betterdesk-release-workflow.mdc`](betterdesk-release-workflow.mdc). Default remains Chesster-only; severity or “critical” does **not** authorize UNITRONIX targeting.

## Commit + push after panel-relevant rule/doc changes

Follow [`panel-update-commit-push.mdc`](panel-update-commit-push.mdc): push target is **`origin/dev` on Chesster1981**, never UNITRONIX.
